  "term": "Wechsler Intelligence Scale for Children",
  "definition": "The Wechsler Intelligence Scale for Children is an individually given psychological test used to measure the cognitive abilities of children ages 6 through 16 years 11 months. It evaluates current verbal and nonverbal functioning, including verbal comprehension, perceptual reasoning, working memory, and processing speed.",
